---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import Stage from "../../components/Stage.astro";
---
<Base title="Dropdown: an accessible actions menu" description="iVOLT dropdown: an actions menu built on details/summary, promoted to the ARIA menu button pattern with arrow-key navigation. Not for site navigation.">
  <article class="docs-prose" data-enriched>
    <h1>Dropdown (actions menu)</h1>
    <p>A small menu of actions attached to a button. Without JavaScript the native <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> opens and closes and the items are ordinary buttons and links. With it, the menu follows the ARIA menu button pattern. This is not a navigation menu: use links, a disclosure or the drawer for that.</p>
    <p class="docs-meta"><strong>CSS:</strong> <code>css/components/dropdown.css</code>. <strong>JS:</strong> <code>@intervolutions/ivolt/dropdown</code> or <code>auto.js</code>.</p>
    <Stage primary name="dropdown/basic" title="A menu under its trigger" minHeight="16rem" />

    <Section title="Options" num={1}>
      <div class="docs-scroller">
        <table><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Attribute</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td><code>placement</code></td><td><code>data-iv-placement</code></td><td><code>bottom-start</code> (<code>bottom-end</code> aligns to the end edge)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>closeOnSelect</code></td><td><code>data-iv-close-on-select</code></td><td><code>true</code></td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
      </div>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Keyboard" num={2}>
      <p>Enter, Space or Down on the button opens the menu and focuses the first item; Up/Down move with wrap-around, Home/End jump; Escape closes and returns focus; Tab closes without trapping.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Events" num={3}>
      <p><code>iv:open</code>/<code>iv:close</code> (cancelable) and <code>iv:opened</code>/<code>iv:closed</code>; <code>open()</code>, <code>close()</code>, <code>toggle()</code>, <code>isOpen</code>.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Common mistakes" num={4}>
      <ul><li>Using <code>role="menu"</code> for a list of navigation links.</li><li>Menus with more than about seven items; use a page instead.</li></ul>
    </Section>
    <Section title="Without JavaScript" num={5}>
      <p>The served markup is a <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> whose <code>&lt;summary&gt;</code> is the trigger, so the menu opens and closes natively and every item is a working button or link. The script adds the menu-button roles, arrow keys, focus return and closing on outside clicks; <code>destroy()</code> puts the served HTML back.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Customising" num={6}>
      <p>Locals: <code>--iv-dropdown-min-width</code> and <code>--iv-dropdown-offset</code> (the gap between trigger and menu). Use <code>iv-dropdown--end</code> or <code>data-iv-placement="bottom-end"</code> when the trigger sits at the end of a row, so the menu opens inwards.</p><pre tabindex="0"><code>.toolbar .iv-dropdown &#123; --iv-dropdown-min-width: 14rem; &#125;</code></pre>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Dropdown, select or navigation?" num={7}>
      <p>A dropdown runs actions: rename, duplicate, delete. To choose a value use a native <a href="/components/form">select</a>, or the <a href="/components/picker">picker</a> when there are many options; to list pages use links, a <a href="/components/disclosure">disclosure</a> or the <a href="/components/drawer">drawer</a>. Screen readers announce a menu as an application widget, which is wrong for a list of links.</p>
    </Section>


    <Section title="Class index" num={8}>
      <p>Parts and modifiers of this family that the examples above do not show. The full list per stylesheet lives in the <a href="/reference">reference</a>.</p>
      <div class="docs-scroller docs-class-index">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>iv-dropdown--end</code></td><td>Aligns the menu with the end edge of the trigger.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </Section>
  </article>
</Base>
